# Arc Supabase migration conventions

Match the existing `*_arc_stories.sql` pattern.

- File name: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_short_description.sql`. Start with a comment explaining the object and its relation to existing tables.
- Every table:
  - `id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()`
  - FKs reference `public.<table> (id)` with explicit `on delete`.
  - `created_at timestamptz not null default now()`; add `updated_at` if mutable.
  - Sensible `not null default`s on flags; `unique (...)` where duplicates are impossible.
- Indexes on every column the app filters/sorts by (e.g. `published_at desc nulls last`, `category`, `is_live`).
- ALWAYS enable RLS and add explicit policies:
```sql
  alter table public.<t> enable row level security;
  create policy "Anyone can read live rows"
    on public.<t> for select
    to anon, authenticated
    using (is_live = true);
```
- Public read limited to published rows (`is_live = true`). Writes happen server-side via the service-role key (bypasses RLS) — do NOT add anon write policies unless a real user action needs it.
- NEVER disable RLS to "make it work." NEVER hand-edit an applied migration — write a new one.
